sweet-fb-skip (lowclk 2026-11-14, group A item A5-3; research docs/research/160-kernel-cpu-users-lskdd-boot-reads.md s.1.1 and U2; tracker L-25): AppleCLCD::present skips the CPU panel copy when nothing it reads has changed since the last copy. NO HARDWARE ACCESS: the panel memory is written by the same memcpy as before, only less often; no register, no firmware command.
Why [obs from research 160]: the panel copy is the "thread call kernel-high #1" thread, 64-66 s of CPU per boot (37 presents/s x 1.7-2.3 ms); the row says "empty presents counted" but not how many are unchanged (U2).
Unchanged-since-last-copy signal [read from source, not pixels]: (1) the swap record is byte-identical except the swap id (get32(rec, 0x50), the "swap %u" of the existing log); (2) the seed of every layer surface is the same (SweetSurface state page +0xc, bumped by sweet_surface_seed_out on every write-unlock, SweetSurface.cpp trapUnlock; read by the new sweet_surface_seed_peek); (3) the Mali submitted seqno is the same (sweet_mali_seq_peek, patch 0186; every job has its seqno at submit, also parked ones, patch 0227). (2) covers CPU writers that lock/unlock the IOSurface, (3) covers GPU writers. Not covered: a CPU writer that writes the mapped surface without a lock (the IOSurface API requires the lock) [guess: none on this root]; hence the refresh below.
Always copied [read from source]: the first frame; the present after any power change (RequestPowerChange) or QR hold (fForceCopy, atomic exchange); while the kernel console is not muted (it draws into the panel memory, sweet_console_muted); Mali not up or dead (no GPU signal); the present after a copy that ran while the GPU was busy or during which a job was submitted (that copy may have shown half a frame); every 150th unchanged present in a row (bounded staleness, counted as "refresh"). There is no mode change or brightness path in this driver (geometry is set once in start(); GetGammaTable/brightness are absent), so no event beyond those exists to force a copy.
Boot-arg sweetfb_skip: 0 = off, today's behaviour (no decision, no counting); 1 = skip (default); 2 = count only (decide, log, always copy: the "count first" step); other values = GAP row and 1.
Log (rule 7): one row at the first present naming the mode; every 10 s of presents `SWEET FB: panel skip (10 s, mode M): presents N copied C skipped S would-skip W; why first/forced/console/nosig/gpubusy/rec/seed/gpu/refresh (sums since boot); unchanged U skipped T`; the existing sweetfb_copytime row gets `unchanged U skipped T` appended.
Host test: tools/test_sweetfb_skip.py compiles the added pure function sweet_fb_skip_why from this patch text and checks every reason and priority, that only the swap id is ignored, each of the 4 layer seeds, the seqno and the refresh bound, then text checks of the hooks (force events, loop gate, record after copy, GAP, count-only) with a mutant per check. Not run on hardware.
